            <physDesc xml:id="physDesc_N202CD">
               <extent xml:id="extent_N202CE">12 pages</extent>
               <dimensions unit="cm" xml:id="dimensions_N202D1">34 x 26.5</dimensions>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_N202D4">3 bifolios. Written in brown ink. Paper: 14 staves. First and last page blank. Contains the following songs: "N<rend xml:id="idm27" rend="sup">o.</rend> 20 Udfrielsen af Ægypten" (HartW 376); "N<rend xml:id="idm28" rend="sup">o.</rend> 22 Lovgivningen paa Sinai" (HartW 388); "N<rend xml:id="idm29" rend="sup">o.</rend> 33 David og Goliath"; "N<rend xml:id="idm30" rend="sup">o.</rend> 34 Davids Seiers-Sang" (HartW 375); "N<rend xml:id="idm31" rend="sup">o.</rend> 57 Johannes den Døber" (HartW 377); "N<rend xml:id="idm32" rend="sup">o.</rend> 59 Herrens Fristelse" (HartW 385); "N<rend xml:id="idm33" rend="sup">o.</rend> 69 Jairi Datter" (HartW 379); "N<rend xml:id="idm34" rend="sup">o.</rend> 93 Kammersvenden fra Morland" (HartW 381); and "N<rend xml:id="idm35" rend="sup">o.</rend> 64 Peders Apostel-Kald" (HartW 378). Contrary to Hartmann's habit, the texts are in Latin script.</physMedium>
            </physDesc>
            <notesStmt xml:id="notesStmt_N202FA">
               <annot type="source_description" xml:id="annot_b2bef138">
                  <p xml:id="idm38">"David and Goliath" is the only song in this manuscript, which remained unpublished.</p>
